 "DONE","2026-08-08","SHIPPED, with the denominator CHOSEN rather than asked about again - the user said not to wait for confirmation. This row had correctly flagged the real obstacle: a progress bar needs a BOUNDED range and raw P&L has none (an unbounded CSP loss, a long option at +400%). Resolved by picking RETURN ON CAPITAL AT RISK - what the leg actually cost - because it is the only measure defined for EVERY leg type in that table: debit spreads, naked longs and stock alike. Percent-of-max-profit reads better but is undefined for anything with unlimited upside, and a bar that blanks out on half the book is worse than no bar. Bounded by CLIPPING rather than by changing the measure: the Streamlit ProgressColumn spans -100% (premium fully lost, which IS the real floor on a long option) to +100% (a double); anything beyond still prints its true number in the label while the bar simply pins full. Applied to the flat all-positions table in dashboard.py; dashboard restarted and serving HTTP 200",
