(168,"2026-08-08","Claude","Research","Inflation DIRECTION alone splits asset returns - the growth axis does not",
 "Fell out of the ID 131 test. Across 832 months the two falling-inflation quadrants look near-identical and the two rising-inflation quadrants look near-identical, which means the Clocks second axis is close to noise",
 "REJECTED","2026-08-08",
 "TESTED ON TOTAL RETURNS AND THE RULE IS REJECTED - but the underlying finding survives. tools/test_inflation_rule.py, 1,169 months 1926-2023 from Shiller ie_data (price AND dividends, plus CPI and the 10y from the same source so nothing can disagree about vintages), CPI lagged 2m. THE FINDING HOLDS: equities earn 12.95%/yr when inflation is falling against 8.58% when it is rising, a +4.37%/yr gap - WIDER on total return than the +4.20% price-only version. THE RULE FAILS: switching to bonds on rising inflation costs -1.71%/yr versus always-stocks (t=-1.35), and both halves agree (-3.34%, -0.09%). CAGR 8.91% vs 10.16%, Sharpe a dead heat at 0.40, drawdown -71.6% vs -81.8% - not worth 1.7%/yr when both are catastrophic. WHY IT LOOKED GOOD BEFORE: without dividends, rising-inflation equities appeared to earn ~1.5%/yr so nearly anything beat them; their true total return is 8.58%, comfortably above bonds 4.93%, so the switch was never justified. The whole apparent edge WAS the missing dividend - precisely the caveat recorded when the finding was logged. Written up as ADOPTED.md 12.4b. Keep the descriptive fact as macro CONTEXT; never as a switching signal",
 "-","P2","-"),
(169,"2026-08-08","User","Feature","Dealer scanner: what options are dealers SELLING, where are they positioned, how do they hedge with futures",
 "User: i want a dealer information scanner - what options they are selling, where are they, how are they hedging futures and other info. Do we have a git for this",
 "DONE","2026-08-08",
 "SHIPPED as /dealer, and one line of my own scoping note above was WRONG. True dealer OPTION inventory is indeed not public - every GEX tool on GitHub, ours included, INFERS it from a sign convention and none of them measure it. But I also wrote that dealer FUTURES hedges need paid data, and that is false: the CFTC publishes them free and weekly in the Traders in Financial Futures report, no key required. Built on it - 10 PINNED contracts (S&P, Nasdaq, Russell, VIX, 2Y/10Y/30Y, USD, Yen, Euro), 3 years of weekly history each, one HTTP request for all ten, 6h cache. Codes are pinned rather than name-matched because a name LIKE query returned MICRO E-MINI NASDAQ instead of the main contract - a silently wrong book. Reports net position as a share of open interest AND its percentile in its own history, because dealers are STRUCTURALLY net short equity index futures and the raw level says nothing. Verified live: S&P dealers sit at -33.9% of OI but only the 47th percentile - a vast short that is entirely normal, which is exactly the misreading the percentile prevents. Fixed two defects found in test: ordinals rendered 93th/1th, and the table was 29 cells wide against Telegram 28-cell <pre> limit",
 "-","P1","Streamlit panel + Playwright DOM check still outstanding"),
(170,"2026-08-08","User","Bug","bot_watchdog.ps1 quarantined by antivirus as IDP.Generic",
 "User: my antivirus moved bot_watchdog.ps1 to quarantine, it was infected with IDP.Generic. Do you want it released?",
 "DONE","2026-08-08",
 "NOT A REAL INFECTION, AND MY DESIGN CAUSED IT. Recovered both files from git (HEAD and 00f61e0) and compared - byte-identical to what was written on 08-07, nothing injected. But IDP.Generic is a BEHAVIOURAL detection and the design earned the flag: a .vbs launcher opening a hidden window (WScript.Shell.Run window style 0) -> powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -> WMI process enumeration reading other processes command lines -> a DNS probe to an external host -> a detached hidden process spawn. That is the fingerprint of a dropper with persistence and a check-in; the scanner read the behaviour correctly and only the intent was wrong. ADVISED THE USER NOT TO RELEASE IT: nothing is lost (both files are in git), a released file gets re-flagged on the next scan, and overriding an AV warning to run your own script is a habit not worth building. Replaced instead of argued with - rewritten as pure Python run under pythonw.exe, which removes ALL FOUR triggers (no VBS, no PowerShell, no ExecutionPolicy Bypass, no hidden-window trick) and gets a windowless process natively, which was the point of the VBS in the first place. COLLATERAL FINDING flagged to the user: TelegramBotWatchdog no longer exists as a scheduled task, and NYSE_OffHours_Chain and NYSE_OffsiteBackup are both DISABLED - a disabled EOD task is the exact failure behind row 121",
 "-","P0","-"),
(171,"2026-08-08","User","Security","Audit our own code the way a good antivirus would",
 "User: also think like best antivirus. Prompted by the IDP.Generic quarantine of row 170",
 "DONE","2026-08-08",
 "SCANNED THE WHOLE REPO for the patterns a behavioural engine actually flags. CLEAN: zero ExecutionPolicy Bypass, zero WScript.Shell/VBS launchers, zero base64 or -EncodedCommand, zero DownloadString/IEX, zero shell=True, zero Run-key or Startup-folder persistence, and zero antivirus-tampering calls (Add-MpPreference/Set-MpPreference). The only hits are 12 uses of CREATE_NO_WINDOW / DETACHED_PROCESS, every one of them a legitimate Python subprocess spawn (dashboard, intraday lane, EOD chain) that exists so the user does not get console flashes - the complaint behind row 124. One taskkill /F /PID on a recorded old pid, part of the single-instance guard. CONCLUSION: the VBS+PowerShell watchdog was the only genuinely malware-shaped artefact in the project and it is now gone. Rule adopted: if a script would look like a loader to a scanner, rewrite it rather than excluding it",
 "-","P1","-"),
