 "DELIVERED as /feed - see row 186 for the build and verification. Status was left QUEUED by mistake when 186 was logged (only the Next Step column was rewritten), which is exactly the stale-row failure that makes the sheet untrustworthy; corrected 2026-08-08. Original scoping kept below because the route choice is the useful part of the record: (1) INGEST - the bot is a Bot API client, and a bot cannot read a channel it is not an admin of, so the route is either adding the bot to the channel, or a user-session client (Telethon/Pyrogram, needs api_id/api_hash and stores a session credential), or the channel public web feed. Each has a different cost and privacy profile and the user should pick. (2) LLM - ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is already in api_keys.enc, and row 38 (Ollama, local and free) is BLOCKED on install; free-tier hosted options exist but rate-limit hard. Cheapest correct answer is probably local Ollama for bulk summarisation with the paid key reserved for anything acted on. (3) THE TRAP, per rows 176 and 131: an LLM will happily produce a confident trade idea from a headline, and that is exactly the unmeasured-confidence failure just fixed in the big-move alert. Any idea it emits must be labelled as unvalidated commentary, or scored against forward returns before it is presented as a signal",
