 "GOOGLE FIXED - and I had been wrong twice, both corrected by testing rather than argument. First I claimed the key was the wrong type because it did not start with AIza; the user showed AQ. IS the current AI Studio format. The real causes: (1) gemini-2.0-flash and 2.5-flash are RETIRED for new projects - 2.5 returns 404 no longer available to new users and the 2.0 family returns 429 with no free quota - so a NEW project only gets the current generation; fixed by using the moving alias gemini-flash-latest instead of a pinned version, because pinning is what made a live key look dead. (2) My own test was the second bug: at max_tokens=10 Gemini returns finish_reason=length with content=None because it spends budget REASONING before emitting; at 200 it returns cleanly. Added a 256-token floor for Google so a small caller budget can never fake a dead provider again. Final: Groq PASS 259ms, Google PASS 1231ms, OpenRouter PASS 921ms, Cerebras still HTTP 402 (account billing, not fixable here). INGEST BUILT via t.me/s/<channel>, which Telegram renders server-side for public channels - deliberately chosen over the alternatives: the Bot API cannot read a channel the bot is not admin of, and Telethon would write a SESSION FILE that IS the users Telegram identity, a bad trade for read-only public data in a session spent locking this machine down. The web feed needs no key, no session and no permission. Verified live: 19 posts parsed with timestamps and links, cache honoured, all chunks tag-balanced under the 4096 cap. /feed renders the latest 8 plus an LLM read (two items that matter, one trade idea with its risk, one thing the headlines over-read), and that read is LABELLED as unvalidated commentary rather than a signal - per the row 176 lesson about confident-sounding output with no base rate behind it",
