 "DONE","2026-08-08",
 "INVESTIGATED - AND THE ANSWER IS NO, KEEP IT, because it is the INPUT rather than a copy. Three live readers, two of which are the download lanes themselves: NYSE_OpenBB.py:225 builds the PRIMARY EOD capture universe from sheet openbb_universe (741 names), NYSE_YFin.py:150 does the same for the Yahoo fallback, and dashboard.py:6568 reads sheet bk (592). The decisive measurement: of the 734 tickers captured in options_change over the last 30 days, ZERO are absent from the workbook - every ticker in the database is there BECAUSE the workbook listed it. Deriving the universe from the DB would therefore be circular, and worse, it would FREEZE the universe: no new ticker could ever enter the system, and adding names is precisely what the workbook is for. Coverage is 93.6%; the 50 uncovered names are legitimately uncapturable (crypto pairs BTC-USD/ADA-USD/DOGE-USD have no US options chains, plus thin names and bond ETFs), so the file is mildly aspirational, which is harmless. NOTED FOR TIDYING, not done without permission: three copies sit in the folder (ticker_universe.xlsx, - Copy.xlsx, and a July backup) but only the first is read by anything, and sheets ticker_universe and Whole_universe hold an identical 94 names - the kind of drift that eventually gets the wrong sheet edited",
