 "DONE","2026-08-08",
 "SEARCHED CURRENT SOURCES RATHER THAN ANSWERING FROM MEMORY. Community consensus for 2026 matches what was already wired: Groq for speed, Google AI Studio for the biggest free context (1M tokens on Gemini Flash), OpenRouter for model variety on one key, Cerebras for raw daily volume (1M tokens/day). Groq free tier measured limits: 30 req/min, 14,400 req/day, 500k tokens/day on llama-3.1-8b-instant - far more than a news channel needs. Canonical maintained directory is github.com/cheahjs/free-llm-api-resources (auto-updated rate limits), with open-free-llm-api/awesome-freellm-apis as a larger but noisier list. THE FINDING THAT ACTUALLY MATTERS AND CHANGES A RECOMMENDATION: on most no-credit-card free tiers YOUR PROMPTS TRAIN THE MODEL - that is what funds them. Groq, OpenRouter and Cerebras publish clearer no-training positions; Google AI Studios FREE tier uses data for product improvement, which is exactly the trade-off this user should decide knowingly given they spent the same session locking filesystem scope down. Practical split recorded: public news text (the Kobeissi channel) is fine on any of them; anything containing POSITIONS or the book must not go to a training-on-by-default free tier. Groq stays primary - fast, ample limits, no-training - and Google remains wired but should be pointed at public news only",
